        72: "Settings → Plugins also lists the plugins shipped with pi-prjcts (`tasks`, `simulator`) before they are loaded, from static metadata in `src/bundled-plugins.ts`; nothing is imported to list them. Each shows one of four states: `available` (not configured), `configured` (in `plugins.json` or `PI_PROJECTS_PLUGINS`, awaiting a restart), `loaded` or `failed` (with the loader's error). **Add to host config** appends the absolute path of that shipped directory to `plugins.json` by catalog id only, keeps every other entry and key as it was, does nothing when the directory is already configured, and refuses an unreadable `plugins.json` or a name an external plugin already loaded. Adding a plugin does not load it or restart the host. **Restart host and enable** asks before interrupting work in all projects. It restarts the serving host on its running revision without fetching or deploying, then reads the catalog again. A changed checkout or unverifiable launch is refused. The Host agent can read the catalog (`plugin-catalog`) but cannot add plugins or confirm a restart. There is no remote catalog, URL install or path input in this interface; external plugins are still configured by hand as above.",
